      {
        "n": "Slow Hand Clutches (R)",
        "s": "2026-10-29T02:00:00Z",
        "e": "2026-10-29T03:00:00Z",
        "d": "FM: We think a lot about murmur, what Du Bois calls “the murmur of ages,” and we think about murmuration, that amazing shift of social formation that birds do in the air.\nSS: Like over Brighton pier.\nFM: “Murmuration” is a cool word because it bears the trace of the sound. It’s beautiful when you watch those movements, but it’s even more beautiful when you hear them. The internal differentiation of the swarm is absolute wealth.\nExtract from Refusing Completion: A Conversation\nFred Moten, Stefano Harney, and Stevphen Shukaitis",
